    Problem : Print all elements of a 3×3 matrix using a single pointer. (Matrix stored in row‑major order)
    Solution:
        int mat[3][3] = {{1,2,3}, {4,5,6}, {7,8,9}};
        int *p = &mat[0][0];   // pointer to the first element
        for(int i = 0; i < 9; i++) {
            printf("%d ", *(p + i));
        }

14. Dangling Pointer Prevention
    Problem : Allocate memory, assign it to a pointer, free the memory, and immediately set the pointer to NULL to avoid a dangling pointer.
    Solution:
        int *p = (int*)malloc(sizeof(int));
        *p = 100;
        free(p);
        p = NULL;   // now p is not dangling

