1. Basic malloc and free
   Problem : Allocate memory for a single integer, store a value, print it, and free the memory.
   Solution:
        int *ptr = (int*)malloc(sizeof(int));
        if (ptr == NULL) {
            printf("Allocation failed\n");
            return 1;
        }
        *ptr = 100;
        printf("Value : %d\n", *ptr);
        free(ptr);
